      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "iterative is the lowest-power family (shared datapath, 1 rotation/cycle). To hit 50 MSPS it needs Fmax >= 50 MHz, which is very likely for N in 12..20. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) is the binding trade-off: N and the guard bits set accuracy_bits, while data_width sets the output LSB. Sweeping N 12..20 and guards maps the power-vs-accuracy curve; rounding=round typically buys ~0.5 bit of accuracy at small power cost, so both are kept."
    },
